"""Hand-drawn 8x10 proportional pixel typeface for the session list.

PLFONT_8x10 is the fallback list font used by the Winamp-2.x-style skin
engine for every third-party skin that does not supply its own list font.
It aims for a tidy 1980s terminal / LCD hybrid feel: crisp, slightly
squarish, and confident rather than a bland default bitmap font.

Each glyph is a cell of exactly 10 rows by 8 columns, top row first.
``'#'`` marks ink, ``'.'`` marks no ink; no other characters appear.
Column 0 and column 7 of every glyph are always blank, reserved so a
1-pixel halo can be composited around the glyph later without touching
the neighbouring cell.

Metrics (row 0 is the top of the cell, row 9 the bottom):

- Baseline: row 7.
- Capitals and digits: rows 1..7 (cap height 7).
- Lowercase x-height: rows 3..7 (x-height 5).
- Lowercase ascenders (b d f h k l, t a little shorter): start at row 1
  (t at row 2).
- Descenders (g j p q y, and the comma/semicolon tail): rows 8..9.

Keys are every printable ASCII character (code points 32..126 inclusive)
plus ``'…'`` (U+2026 HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS), 96 entries in total.
"""

